<helpdocument version="1.0">
<meta>
<topic id="textscalc01func_bitlshiftxml" indexer="include" status="PUBLISH">
<title id="tit" xml-lang="en-US">BITLSHIFT</title>
<filename>/text/scalc/01/func_bitlshift.xhp</filename>
</topic>
</meta>
<body>
<bookmark xml-lang="en-US" branch="index" id="bm_id3160501">
<bookmark_value>BITLSHIFT function</bookmark_value>
<bookmark_value>bitwise left shift</bookmark_value>
</bookmark>
<bookmark xml-lang="en-US" branch="hid/SC_HID_FUNC_BITLSHIFT" id="bm_id3160502" localize="false"/>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3160501" xml-lang="en-US" level="2" l10n="U"><variable id="bitlshift"><link href="text/scalc/01/func_bitlshift.xhp">BITLSHIFT</link>
</variable></paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160503" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><ahelp hid="HID_FUNC_BITLSHIFT">Bitwise left shift of an integer value.</ahelp> The bits of <emph>Number</emph> are shifted to the left by <emph>Shift</emph> positions, equivalent to multiplying by 2 raised to the power of <emph>Shift</emph>.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3160504" xml-lang="en-US" level="3" l10n="U">Syntax</paragraph>
<paragraph role="code" id="par_id3160505" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U">BITLSHIFT(Number; Shift)</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160506" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><emph>Number</emph> is the integer value to be shifted. It must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than 2^48 (281474976710656).</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160507" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><emph>Shift</emph> is the number of bit positions to shift. A positive value shifts left; a negative value shifts right (the direction is reversed).</paragraph>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3160508" xml-lang="en-US" level="3" l10n="U">Remarks</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160509" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U">If <emph>Shift</emph> is 0, <emph>Number</emph> is returned unchanged.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160510" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U">If <emph>Shift</emph> is greater than or equal to 64 (or less than or equal to -64), the result is 0.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160511" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><emph>Number</emph> is truncated to an integer before the operation. Non-integer, negative, or out-of-range values for <emph>Number</emph>, or non-finite values for <emph>Shift</emph>, return an error (Err:502).</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160512" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U">Example: decimal 1 is binary <quote>1</quote>. BITLSHIFT(1; 2) shifts left by 2, giving binary <quote>100</quote>, which is decimal 4.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3160513" xml-lang="en-US" level="3" l10n="U">Example</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160514" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><item type="input">=BITLSHIFT(1; 2)</item> returns 4.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160515" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><item type="input">=BITLSHIFT(1; -2)</item> returns 0 because a negative shift reverses direction and the value is shifted right, shifting the only bit out.</paragraph>
<embed href="text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#siehe"/>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160516" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><link href="text/scalc/01/func_bitrshift.xhp" name="BITRSHIFT">BITRSHIFT</link>.</paragraph>
</body>
</helpdocument>
